# Line-ending policy.
#
# This repo is often cloned on Windows and then built into a Linux container.
# Without this file, git converts LF to CRLF on checkout, which breaks any file
# the container executes or parses:
#   - entrypoint.sh gets "#!/bin/sh\r", and the kernel fails with the very
#     misleading "exec /entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory"
#   - supervisord.conf / nginx.conf pick up stray \r inside directive values
#
# Forcing LF for these files makes a Windows clone build correctly on Linux.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh      text eol=lf
*.conf    text eol=lf
*.py      text eol=lf
*.html    text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.yaml    text eol=lf
*.txt     text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
.env.example text eol=lf

# Never touch binaries
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.sqlite3 binary
